  <!-- About -->
  <data name="About.Title"><value>About</value></data>
  <data name="About.Version"><value>Version {0}</value></data>
  <data name="About.WhatItIs"><value>Neyra Optimizer is a local performance tuning utility for Windows 10 and Windows 11.</value></data>
  <data name="About.WhatItIsNot"><value>It is NOT an antivirus, NOT a replacement for Windows Security, NOT a driver updater, and NOT an overclocking tool. It makes no guaranteed performance claims; every reported number comes from actual measurements on your machine.</value></data>
  <data name="About.PrivacyNote"><value>Neyra Optimizer works fully offline. No telemetry is sent anywhere. Support bundles contain anonymized technical info only and are generated only when you ask.</value></data>

  <!-- Help/Safety -->
  <data name="Help.Title"><value>Help &amp; Safety</value></data>
  <data name="Help.HowRollbackWorks"><value>How rollback works</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RollbackBody"><value>Before any batch, Neyra writes an Optimization Snapshot listing every previous value. Restore Center can reverse those exact changes individually. If System Restore is enabled a Windows restore point is also offered. Snapshots live under ProgramData\NeyraOptimizer\Snapshots with SHA-256 integrity manifests, so Emergency Restore works even if other app state is damaged.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.WhatWeNeverTouch"><value>What Neyra will never modify</value></data>
  <data name="Help.NeverTouchBody"><value>Windows Security / Defender / Firewall, RPC and core boot services, storage/display/audio/input drivers, authentication, Windows Update security dependencies and recovery components. Rules targeting these are rejected before reaching any Windows API.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.SupportBundle"><value>Create support bundle</value></data>
  <data name="Help.BundleContents"><value>The bundle contains: anonymized OS/CPU/RAM/disk summary, recent structured logs, optimization history metadata, snapshot metadata (no credentials, no personal files). Review the list before exporting.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.DiagMode"><value>Restart in Diagnostics (read-only) mode</value></data>

  <!-- Emergency -->
  <data name="Emergency.Title"><value>Emergency Restore</value></data>
  <data name="Emergency.Body"><value>This minimal window reads snapshots directly from disk with integrity checks. It stays usable even if the main interface has problems.</value></data>

